Now I have all the information needed. Here's the full academic audit:

---

## 🧪 Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 | **Language:** C# / .NET 10 | **Category:** Integration (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 2           | 2              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 1           | 4              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **7**          |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**Smell:** Sleepy Test (testsmells.org)  
**Location:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← blocks for 3 seconds
```

**Why it's a smell even in integration tests:** `Thread.Sleep` is never a reliable synchronization primitive. It introduces non-determinism (too short → flaky; too long → slow suite) regardless of integration scope.

**Fix:**
```csharp
// Poll or use an async wait with timeout
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI builds; suite slows linearly as more sleepy tests are added.

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (a.k.a. Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Unknown Test / Empty Test (testsmells.org)  
**Location:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← No assertion — passes even if data is silently corrupted
}
```

**Fix:**
```csharp
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

var users = _repository.ListAll();
Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — test greenlights a broken bulk path as long as no exception is thrown.

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Conditional Test Logic (testsmells.org)  
**Location:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Why it matters:** One branch is never exercised (the test inserts a plain `User`, so the `PremiumUser` branch is dead code). This hides a testing gap.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden gap — the `PremiumUser` path is never actually tested.

---

#### 🟢 LOW — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Assertion Roulette (testsmells.org, extended catalog)  
**Locations:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (4 assertions, no messages), `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` (2), `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` (2), `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` (1 — not triggered, listed for completeness).

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);       // which failed?
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Calibration note:** With only 3–4 assertions per method and descriptive test names, MSTest's failure output usually suffices. Severity stays **Low** for this suite size.

**Fix (optional but good practice):**
```csharp
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name mismatch after insert");
```

---

### ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (well-designed tests)

| Test | Why it's good |
|------|---------------|
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single concern, clear arrange-act-assert, explicit null-assert |
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Focused mutation test, minimal setup |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Exercises concurrency with a concrete assertion on count |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Self-documenting count (3 inserts → assert 3) — not a Magic Number |

The fixture setup using an in-memory SQLite connection is **not** flagged as Mystery Guest because it's hermetic and explicit — no external resource dependency.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix Effort | Impact |
|----------|-------|-----------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free (`BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`) | ~1 min | Eliminates false-pass risk |
| 2 | Sleepy Test (`NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`) | ~10 min | Removes flakiness + 3s from suite |
| 3 | Conditional Test Logic (`GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`) | ~5 min | Uncovers dead branch, adds real coverage |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette (multiple) | ~5 min | Improves failure diagnostics |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 7 tests are clean. The three problematic tests each exhibit a distinct, well-known academic smell. Fixing priorities 1–3 will materially improve suite reliability; priority 4 is polish.
